  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.611,
            0.068,
            0.815,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The World of Numbers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.855,
            0.068,
            0.883,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "47"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.885,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "fractions as negative fractions. Note that in a negative fraction, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r } { \\longleftarrow } \\end{array}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sign can also be placed with either the numerator or denominator, as follows: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } = { \\frac { - 1 } { 5 } } = { \\frac { 1 } { - 5 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.181,
            0.885,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we combine all integers and all fractions (both positive and negative), we get the set of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rational Numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", denoted by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { Q }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (for quotient)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.239,
            0.884,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "rational number",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is defined as any number that can be expressed in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are integers and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q \\neq 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.314,
            0.399,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.351,
            0.863,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you explain why we need "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q \\neq 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in the definition of a rational number?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.398,
            0.781,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We must make some important observations at this stage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.435,
            0.886,
            0.56
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All rational numbers can be written in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{p}{q},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are integers and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q \\neq 0 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . For example, 5 and –10 can be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { - 1 0 } { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , respectively. What this means is that the rational numbers also include the natural numbers, whole numbers and integers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.561,
            0.886,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rational numbers do not have a unique representation in the form "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { p } { q } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where p and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are integers and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q   \\neq   0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . For example, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-\\frac{1}{3} = -\\frac{2}{6} = -\\frac{3}{9} = -\\frac{10}{30} = -\\frac{2026}{6078}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and so on. These are equivalent rational numbers (or equivalent fractions). This fact allows us to freely divide any common factor between the numerator and the denominator of a given fraction. The resulting fraction is then equivalent to the original one. For example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 2 } { 3 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is equivalent "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{10}{6} \\frac{2}{5}."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Here, we have divided both the numerator and the denominator by 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.141,
            0.82,
            0.886,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The common understanding is that when we say that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a rational number, or when we represent "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { p } { q }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " on the number line, we assume that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q \\neq 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " have no common factors other than"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
